Z||000000||jch82||09-16-2001||01:35 AM||||I am just trying to get some info on different engine setups and somebody suggested this one. Has anyone used this rebuild kit for the 2.8?? If so, what were your likes/dislikes? How much of an upgrade is it in terms of acceleration? 0-60 times, 1/4mi times?? <P>Any and all info is greatly appreciated!Thanks!!<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82(sig).jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||09-16-2001||04:56 AM||||Eh...Don't know what is so "performance" about it.  Forged Pistons?  If you'd like to force some air or NOS into the engine...is good.  Crane cam?...I personally wasn't happy with it in my 3.1 conversion.<P>You'll need $500+ worth of machine work too...so now you are approaching some other conversion that may yield better performance.<P>How many horsies are you looking for?  I'd say that kit is good for 10-20 above stock.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||09-16-2001||01:08 PM||||I agree... That "performance" rebuild kit isn't going to do much of anything in terms acceration.  I believe those forged pistons are 9.5:1 compression, but that is a very small gain hp-wise.  If you want a little more snort for your buck, I'd go with a 3.1 stoker.  The extra cost isn't much.||||reg||1
Z||000003||SLYGUY||09-16-2001||07:27 PM||||I've seen where people have stated that they have a 3.1 or a 3.4 . Even a 3800 Series II. How difficult was this to shoehorn in? Did ANYTHING bolt up or was this an entire fabrication thing? <P>I'd like to see around 200 horses. Is this possible with the 2.8?<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
